g of the preselector.<br>\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=17z8W1TyoE8\">YouTube</a></p>\n<div class=\"embed embed-youtube\"><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/17z8W1TyoE8\" title=\"YouTube\" allowfullscreen referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\"></iframe><p class=\"embed-fallback\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=17z8W1TyoE8\">Watch on YouTube</a></p></div>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1363714470984450051\">https://x.com/i/status/1363714470984450051</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1753913095385190624</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1753913095385190624\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-03T22:47:22Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1753914072955842924":{"a":"<p>Quite a lot of satellite work is just receiving and this radio was amazing for use with CW (Morse), RTTY (teletype), and SSTV (fax) over satellites. Quiet receiver coupled with an early GaAsFET amp from Industrial Communication Engineers worked very well.<br>\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cjiTUzcwYqM\">YouTube</a></p>\n<div class=\"embed embed-youtube\"><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/cjiTUzcwYqM\" title=\"YouTube\" allowfullscreen referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\"></iframe><p class=\"embed-fallback\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cjiTUzcwYqM\">Watch on YouTube</a></p></div>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1753913095385190624\">https://x.com/i/status/1753913095385190624</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1753914072955842924</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1753914072955842924\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-03T22:51:15Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1753914803188273451":{"a":"<p>I replaced the FT-401 with a FT-101 seen above. Much more reliable. The FT-401 literally would catch on fire during operation at times. Very poorly made. It used the first fiberglass PCB in a radio. Tube heat cracked the traces which changed impedances suddenly in HV circuits.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1753914072955842924\">https://x.com/i/status/1753914072955842924</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1753914803188273451</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1753914803188273451\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-03T22:54:09Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1753929174392148164":{"a":"<p>Thank You @IAmAlanWalker for a decade of beautiful music and concerts and here&#x27;s to many many more decades to come. -- #W41k3r #13905</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GtKgt8Q4rNk\">YouTube</a></p>\n<div class=\"embed embed-youtube\"><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/GtKgt8Q4rNk\" title=\"YouTube\" allowfullscreen referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\"></iframe><p class=\"embed-fallback\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GtKgt8Q4rNk\">Watch on YouTube</a></p></div>","m":"<h1>Post 1753929174392148164</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1753929174392148164\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-03T23:51:16Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><